 "cells": [
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "# Data Types\n\n> Verified against crush-ast `d04bc60a` (2026-10-29).\n\nCrush is dynamically typed at run time, with a **static checker** that catches\nobvious mismatches at compile time when you add type annotations. This chapter\ncovers the values you can build today.\n\n## Primitive types\n\n| Type | Literal | Notes |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| Int | `42`, `-7`, `0x2A`, `0b101` | 64-bit signed; overflow is a runtime error |\n| Float | `3.14` | 64-bit IEEE 754. No exponent literals (`1.5e3` is a parse error) |\n| String | `\"hello\"`, `'hello'` | `len` counts **bytes** |\n| Bool | `true`, `false` | |\n| Null | `null` | absence of a value |\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let count = 42\nlet pi = 3.14\nlet name = \"Alice\"\nlet active = true\nlet nothing = null\nprint(count)\nprint(pi)\nprint(name)\nprint(active)\nprint(nothing)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:19",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "42\n3.14\nAlice\ntrue\nnull\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "### Numbers\n\n`+ - * / %` work on `Int` and `Float`. Mixing the two promotes to `Float`.\n`/` on two `Int`s is **integer division**:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-2",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(10 / 4)\nprint(10.0 / 4)\nprint(1 + 2.5)\nprint(7 % 3)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:46",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "2\n2.5\n3.5\n1\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Dividing by zero is a **runtime error** (`[runtime] division by zero`), for\n`Float` too (there is no `inf` or `NaN`). It is raised by the VM rather than thrown\nas a Crush value, so `try`/`catch` does not intercept it.\n\n`Int` arithmetic is checked: a result outside `i64` stops the program with\n`[runtime] arithmetic overflow`. It never wraps.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    let big = 9223372036854775807\n    print(big + 1)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:69",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a run-time error",
      "expect_error": "arithmetic overflow"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "### Strings\n\nConcatenate with `+`. Adding a number to a string converts the number:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-4",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let first = \"Ada\"\nlet last = \"Lovelace\"\nprint(first + \" \" + last)\nprint(\"Count: \" + 42)\nprint(\"Pi is \" + 3.14)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:78",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "Ada Lovelace\nCount: 42\nPi is 3.14\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-9",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "`len(s)` is the byte length and `s[i]` yields a one-character string (a negative\nindex counts from the end). The standard library's `str.*` capabilities add\n`str.split`, `str.trim`, `str.to_upper`, `str.substring` and friends — see\n[Standard Library](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/stdlib.html). Strings have no methods: `s.to_upper()` is refused\n(`not available in this host: to_upper`); call `str.to_upper(s)`.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let s = \"hello\"\nprint(len(s))\nprint(s[1])\nprint(s[-1])\nprint(str.to_upper(s))\nprint(str.substring(s, 1, 3))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:99",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "5\ne\no\nHELLO\nel\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-11",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "The slice syntax `s[1:3]` is for arrays only; on a string it compiles but fails\nat run time (`expected array, got str`). Use `str.substring`.\n\n## Collections\n\n### Arrays\n\nOrdered, mixed-type, zero-indexed. Index, assign by index, and `len`:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-6",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let numbers = [10, 20, 30]\nprint(numbers[0])\nnumbers[1] = 99\nprint(numbers)\nprint(len(numbers))\n\nlet nested = [[1, 2], [3]]\nprint(nested[0][1])\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:126",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "10\n[10, 99, 30]\n3\n2\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-13",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Append with `array.push(arr, value)` or the method form `arr.push(value)`; `+`\njoins two arrays:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let a = [1, 2]\na.push(3)\narray.push(a, 4)\nprint(a)\nprint([1] + [2])\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:148",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "[1, 2, 3, 4]\n[1, 2]\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-15",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Iterate with `for`:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "for item in [\"a\", \"b\"] {\n    print(item)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:164",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "a\nb\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-17",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "`array.pop(a)` removes and returns the last element, `a.append(v)` is an alias for\n`push`, and slices `a[start:end]` work (end exclusive):\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-9",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let a = [1, 2, 3, 4]\nlet last = array.pop(a)\nprint(last)\nprint(a)\nprint(a[0:2])\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:179",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "4\n[1, 2, 3]\n[1, 2]\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-19",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Reading past the end is a runtime error (`array index out of range`), and so is\n`a[-1]` on an empty array; `a[-1]` on a non-empty one is the last element. The\nmethod form `a.pop()` is **not** available (the program is refused with `not\navailable in this host: pop`); call `array.pop(a)`.\n\nNegative slice bounds count from the end, as an index does: with\n`let a = [1, 2, 3, 4]`, `a[1:-1]` is `[2, 3]`, `a[-3:]` is `[2, 3, 4]` and\n`a[:-1]` is `[1, 2, 3]`. (Before crush-ast\n[#254](https://github.com/nixpt/crush-ast/issues/254) they were silently clamped.)\n\n### Objects (maps)\n\nKey–value pairs written `{\"key\": value}`. Keys may be bare identifiers or\nstrings. Read and write fields with **dot notation** or a **string subscript**:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-10",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let person = {\"name\": \"Alice\", \"age\": 30}\nprint(person.name)\nperson.age = 31\nperson.email = \"alice@example.com\"\nprint(person.age)\nprint(person.email)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:209",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "Alice\n31\nalice@example.com\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-21",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Nested objects chain:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-11",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let cfg = {\"db\": {\"port\": 5432}}\nprint(cfg.db.port)\ncfg.db.port = 5433\nprint(cfg.db.port)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:227",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "5432\n5433\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-23",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Objects keep **insertion order**: printing, `for k in obj` and\n`collections.keys(obj)` all list keys in the order they were first set.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-12",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "let person = {\"name\": \"Alice\"}\nperson[\"age\"] = 30\nlet field = \"name\"\nprint(person[field])\nprint(person)\nfor k in person {\n    print(k)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:243",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "Alice\n{name: Alice, age: 30}\nname\nage\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-25",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Reading a key that isn't there is a runtime error (`expected present map key, got\nabsent key`), not `null`. `len(obj)` is rejected (`expected array or string, got\nmap`); count `collections.keys(obj)` instead.\n\n## Structs\n\nDeclare a struct with its field names (optionally with type hints) **on one\nline**, then build one with a literal that names every field, or with\n`new Name()` and assign fields individually:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-13",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "struct Point { x: Float, y: Float }\n\nlet a = Point { x: 1.0, y: 2.0 }\nlet p = new Point()\np.x = 1.5\np.y = 2.5\nprint(a)\nprint(p.x + p.y)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:272",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "{x: 1.0, y: 2.0}\n4.0\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-27",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Structs are **sealed**: writing a field the struct doesn't declare stops the\nprogram (`` `Point` is sealed: it has no field `z` (fields: x, y) ``), and a\nliteral with a missing or unknown field is a compile error. Field type hints are\n**not enforced** at run time today, and an unassigned field reads as `null`.\nMethods, traits, value semantics and `@kind` are in\n[Structs, Methods and Kinds](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/structs.html).\n\nA struct body that spans several lines is still rejected: the parser doesn't skip\nnewlines inside `struct { ... }` (gap `GAP-STRUCT-MULTILINE`, listed in crush-ast's\nCRUSH-192 ticket):\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-14",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "struct Point {\n    x: Float,\n    y: Float\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:301",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "not implemented yet (GAP-STRUCT-MULTILINE); Run shows what happens today"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-29",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Type annotations\n\nYou may annotate variables, parameters and return types with `Int`, `Float`,\n`String`, `Bool`, or `Any`. The compiler checks them statically:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-15",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn double(n: Int) -> Int {\n    return n * 2\n}\nlet label: String = \"answer\"\nprint(label)\nprint(double(21))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:313",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "answer\n42\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-31",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Mismatches are rejected at compile time:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-16",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    let x: Int = \"not a number\"\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:331",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a compile error"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-17",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn double(n: Int) -> Int {\n    return n * 2\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    print(double(\"seven\"))\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:336",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a compile error"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-34",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "Annotations are optional. Not available: generic forms (`Array<Int>`), array\nshorthand (`Int[]`), nullable `T?`, and `Function`/`Array`/`Map` as hint names —\nall fail with a parse or `Unknown type` error.\n\n## Conversion and inspection\n\nThe standard library's `conv.*` capabilities convert between types and report\nthem:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-18",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(conv.to_int(\"42\") + 1)\nprint(conv.to_str(5) + \"x\")\nprint(conv.to_float(2))\nprint(conv.type_of([1]))\nprint(conv.type_of(null))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:352",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "43\n5x\n2.0\narray\nnull\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-36",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "`conv.type_of` returns `int`, `float`, `string`, `bool`, `null`, `array` or\n`map`. There is no `type.of`.\n\n## Conditions must be Bool\n\n`if` and `while` conditions are type-checked: an `Int` or `String` is **not**\nsilently truthy. Compare explicitly (`x != 0`, `s != \"\"`).\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-19",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    if 1 {\n        print(\"yes\")\n    }\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "expected-failure"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/types.md:378",
      "browser": "fail",
      "why": "this example shows a compile error"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-types-md-38",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Comparison\n\n`==`/`!=` compare values of the same type; comparing a string to an int is a\ncompile error (`Cannot compare types string and int`). `1 == 1.0` is `true`.\n\n## Not available yet\n\n| Feature | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `Bytes` literals (`b\"...\"`) | refused: `bytes literals (b\"...\") are not supported yet` |\n| `Error(...)` values | undefined |\n| Optional types `T?`, `??` | not parsed |\n| Enums, type aliases, generics | not in the grammar |\n| `Function` as a type hint | `Unknown type` (function values themselves work: [Closures](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/closures.html)) |\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- **[Variables](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/variables.html)**: scope and mutation\n- **[Operators](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/operators.html)**: the operator reference\n- **[Functions](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/functions.html)**: calls, recursion, hints\n- **[Control Flow](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/control_flow.html)**: loops, `match`, `try`/`catch`\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  }
 ]
}
